            title: 'Maltese Cross',
            subtitle: 'Domino game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Maltese Cross is a domino game played with a double-six set. It takes its name from the tableau layout that resembles a Maltese Cross. The game features a unique two-phase setup where players first build four arms around a central spinner, then add doubles crosswise to complete the cross shape before regular play continues.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'A member of the Cyprus family of domino games, named after the distinctive Maltese Cross pattern formed by the tableau during play.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '2-4 players, individually or in partnerships',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard double-six domino set (28 tiles). For 2 players: 7 tiles each. For 3-4 players: 5-6 tiles each.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard double-six domino set (28 tiles). For 2 players: 7 tiles each. For 3-4 players: 5-6 tiles each.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Tiles are dealt evenly. Remaining tiles form the boneyard.',
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
