          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: "Be the first player to play all your tiles (domino). Score the total pips remaining in opponents' hands.",
          gameplay: 'The player with the highest double sets it as the spinner. Going clockwise, each player must play a tile matching the spinner until four tiles are around it (phase one). A player unable to play draws one tile from the boneyard; if it can play they set it, otherwise they keep it and pass. Once four arms are started, each player must add a double to the end of any arm (crosswise); all four arms must be completed (phase two). After that, doubles are played crosswise and non-doubles in line from the ends of the arms. Play continues until one player dominoes or the game blocks.',
          keyRules: [
            'Highest double starts as spinner in center',
            'Phase one: four tiles around spinner, matching the spinner; draw from boneyard if unable to play',
            'Phase two: add one double to end of each arm (crosswise); all four arms must be completed before free play',
            'After phase two: doubles played crosswise, non-doubles in line from arm ends',
            "First to play all tiles (domino) scores sum of pips in opponents' hands",
            'If blocked, player with lowest total wins and scores (sum of others minus own); game to 60 points',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Try to hold two strong suits that total to seven (such as 2s and 5s). This gives you flexibility with the matador matching rule.',
          intermediate: "The 0-0 (blank-blank) is the most valuable tile - it guarantees a play and can block one end of the train. Save matadors to change the end of the train when you don't have a matching tile.",
          advanced: 'If you have a double, try to set up an arm in phase one that will let you play it in phase two. For example, with the 6-6 double as spinner and you hold 5-6 and 5-5, play 5-6 on the spinner to guarantee playing 5-5 on the next turn.',
          tips: [
            'Leading with the highest double gives you control of setting the spinner',
            "Force opponents to draw by making the train end on values they likely don't have",
            "Save matadors for emergency plays when you're blocked",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
